course: dictionary
lesson: 8078
title: Reluctant and slow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Reluctant means not wanting to do something, so you are slow to start it. «"Reluctant reader" means a child who dislikes or struggles with reading.» A reluctant reader is not lazy about books by accident. They really do not want to read.
explain: Look for clues around the word. If a character drags their feet, sighs, or keeps finding reasons to wait, the author may be showing reluctance without using the word. Ask yourself: does this person want to do it? If not, reluctant may fit.
explain: Reluctant is often followed by "to", as in reluctant to go to bed or reluctant to try new food. A check you can use: put "not keen" into the sentence in place of reluctant. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Reluctant is an adjective, and its comparison forms are more reluctant and most reluctant.
fact: «Reluctant» means not wanting to do something, so you are slow to do it.
fact: «Reluctant to» is a common phrase, as in a child who is reluctant to go to bed.
fact: «"Reluctant reader" means a child who dislikes or struggles with reading.»
fact: A reluctant hero is a character who does not want the adventure at first, but the story shows them facing it anyway.
exercise: «"Reluctant reader" means a child who dislikes or struggles with reading.» What is a reluctant reader? | A child who is very tall | *A child who dislikes or struggles with reading | A child who loves every book | A child who writes stories
exercise: Which word means not wanting to do something, so slow to do it? | Swift | Bright | Eager | *Reluctant
exercise: Ella is reluctant to try new food. What does reluctant tell you about Ella? | She is very keen and rushes to the table | *She does not want to try it, so she is slow to start | She is feeling sleepy | She has lost her plate
test: The hero was reluctant to leave his home, but he set off anyway. What does reluctant mean? | Lost in the woods | Keen and ready to go | Angry and loud | *Not wanting to do it, so slow to start
test: Which phrase describes a child who dislikes reading and is slow to pick up a book? | A happy singer | An eager reader | A fast writer | *A reluctant reader
exam: Which word fits best? «The ___ child dragged his feet all the way to the library.» | Eager | Noisy | *Reluctant | Cheerful
